From 9190fde16c4d5c34667f87c80b15959d32400d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:47:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] wip-kv-residency: A2 (ii) -- the SLIDING window (the
 boundary follows the watermark)

The static window anchored at the end of `-c` only helps once the run reaches it: at 51k tokens in a
-c 262144 cache the whole used extent is still in the tail (measured 8.9 t/s where a depth-anchored
window gave 18.6).  So the resident window is now the newest `W` cells of the USED extent and the
host/VRAM boundary slides forward as the watermark advances.

  ggml-cuda-vmm-region: `ensure_span(off, bytes, host)` maps OR FLIPS: a piece whose backing kind is
    wrong is remapped through a pinned scratch (stage out -> hipMemUnmap -> map the other kind -> stage
    in), with a device synchronise around the unmap.  The table stays one entry per mapping and the VA
    never changes, so captured graphs and every existing data path stay valid.  `vmm_at`/`vmm_next` are
    binary searches now (the slide calls them per cell per batch).
  ggml-cuda.cu: the buft carries the window in CELLS and keeps the slide position (kv_lead_cells,
    monotone) + the VRAM watermark, so a batch only maps the DELTAS -- one cell normally, and one
    unit-sized remap every `unit/nb1` cells (~1900 cells on the 27B, ~3900 on the 35B).  The boundary
    is quantised down to whole map units so a remap is a whole-mapping unmap (the driver refuses
    sub-ranges), and cells between quantised boundaries are simply kept resident a little longer.
  llama-kv-cache.cpp: W cells (not a fixed tail in bytes); DEFAULT W = -c = no spill, i.e. today's
    cache, with the opt-in being what spills.

Measured (1 GPU, gfx1201):
  * text byte-identical to the fully resident arm on 4B (W=1024) and 27B q8_0 -- and byte-identical to
    the pre-slide hash, which is the proof that a remap preserves every staged chunk;
  * 27B Q8_0 -c 262144 at 51 475 tokens (the OOM config): W=49152 -> 18.6 t/s vs 8.9 static and 18.7
    fully resident -- the big context now runs at the small one's speed; W=16384 -> 10.3 (1.19 GiB of
    spill per token, as modelled);
  * 35B-A3B Q8_0 -ncmoe 24 -c 262144 at 5256 tokens: arena 12393 -> 15070 MiB, host-expert residency
    63.3 % -> 77.0 %, slab mapped 13.19 -> 15.81 GiB, prefill 602 -> 615 t/s, decode 64.5 -> 64.9 t/s
    with ZERO spill.  That is Goal A's second half with no cost.

Not for patches/: nothing here is in the delivery set.
